--[[
    Fix HD Inventory Icon Position: restore SortingPlus' highlight overrides,
    dropped by the HD framework's copy of zzz_rax_sortingplus_mcm.script.

    Why this exists:
      HD_Inventory_Icons_Framework ships zzz_rax_sortingplus_mcm.script and wins
      the load-order conflict over SortingPlus' own copy. The framework's copy is
      an older fork and is missing three overrides that SortingPlus still ships:

        ui_inventory.UIInventory:Highlight        -- records that a highlight is up
        ui_inventory.UIInventory:UnHighlight_All  -- only clears when one is up
        utils_ui.UICellItem:Update                -- clears a cell's stale highlight

      The first two are a pair: UnHighlight_All walks every cell in every
      container, and SortingPlus made it a no-op unless a highlight was actually
      set. The third clears a cell's highlight as it is refreshed, so a highlight
      does not linger on a cell that has been recycled for a different item.

    Confidence note, read before trusting this file:
      Unlike the satiety and meat picker fixes, these three were found by
      auditing the framework's forks rather than from a reported symptom. They
      are faithful re-adds of SortingPlus' code, but I have not reproduced a
      user-visible bug caused by their absence -- the likely effects are wasted
      work in UnHighlight_All and highlights outliving their cell. The Update
      override is the one to watch: it runs on every cell refresh, so if
      highlighting misbehaves after this ships, drop this file first.

    Interaction with zzzz_loot_searching.script:
      That file also wraps utils_ui.UICellItem.Highlight, to suppress highlights
      on hidden loot. It loads after this one (zzzz_ sorts after zzz_aaa_), so
      its wrapper ends up outermost. Our Update override calls self:Highlight(),
      which resolves through the class table at call time and therefore reaches
      the loot-searching wrapper -- hidden items stay suppressed.

    Idempotence:
      SortingPlus exposes no marker we can test for, so unlike the other fixes in
      this mod we cannot detect whether its copy already won and skip. All three
      wrappers are written to be harmless if applied twice: setting a flag that
      is already set, a guarded clear that re-checks the same flag, and a
      highlight clear that is already idempotent.
--]]



if not (ui_inventory and ui_inventory.UIInventory and utils_ui and utils_ui.UICellItem) then
    return
end



-- Record that a highlight is up, so UnHighlight_All knows there is work to do.
local base_Highlight = ui_inventory.UIInventory.Highlight
if base_Highlight then
    ui_inventory.UIInventory.Highlight = function(self, sec, bag_id)
        self.highlight_set = true
        return base_Highlight(self, sec, bag_id)
    end
end


-- Skip the full sweep over every cell unless something is actually highlighted.
local base_UnHighlight_All = ui_inventory.UIInventory.UnHighlight_All
if base_UnHighlight_All then
    ui_inventory.UIInventory.UnHighlight_All = function(self)
        if self.highlight_set then
            base_UnHighlight_All(self)
            self.highlight_set = false
        end
    end
end


-- Clear a cell's highlight as it refreshes, so it cannot outlive the item that
-- earned it when the cell is reused.
local base_CellItem_Update = utils_ui.UICellItem.Update
if base_CellItem_Update then
    utils_ui.UICellItem.Update = function(self, obj)
        self:Highlight()
        return base_CellItem_Update(self, obj)
    end
end
